  "summary": "Fix a race condition in `scantxoutset` by zeroing the scan progress counter before clearing the in-progress flag in `CoinsViewScanReserver`. This ensures subsequent scan calls cannot acquire the reservation while observing stale, non-zero progress.",
  "problem": "When overlapping `scantxoutset` RPC calls occur, a new scan can acquire the scan reservation immediately after an old scan unsets `g_scan_in_progress` but before it resets `g_scan_progress`. The new caller's progress check then throws an exception before its reserver records ownership, leaving the node reporting \"Scan already in progress\" on all future calls until the node is restarted.",
